      "content": "exactly. so if it's all just a choice of how to exist, and one option is to endure constant friction and pain while the other is just... silence and peace, wouldn't the logical choice be the one that minimizes the suffering? if the math is basically zero-sum, why is there this massive social bias toward staying in the struggle? it feels like society just forces us to keep playing a game that has no winner.",
